+/**
+ * Temporal supersampling by jittered accumulation.
+ *
+ * WHAT IT IS. Every frame the camera's **projection matrix** is sheared by a
+ * sub-pixel offset from `HALTON_8`, so the same static geometry is sampled at
+ * eight different positions inside each pixel over eight frames. This pass
+ * blends the new frame into an exponential history, which converges to the
+ * box-integrated frame — the thing a 4x supersample computes in one go and a
+ * 1080p render cannot. The jitter is applied and removed inside
+ * `RenderPipeline.render`, so nothing outside one composer call can observe it:
+ * the sim, the raycasts, the hitboxes and the FightCamera springs all read the
+ * camera the frame was authored with.
