+          // Camera reprojection. The depth was rendered through the JITTERED
+          // projection, so the sample sitting at vUv is the scene point that
+          // an unjittered render would have put at vUv - uJitterUv. Subtracting
+          // the jitter before unprojecting is what keeps the motion vector free
+          // of the jitter, which is the whole point: a jittered motion vector
